[Music]  [Applause]  I'm joined at the ftth conference in  Amsterdam by Thomas Renault of Iliad one  of the most innovative providers in  France so much it's really nice to talk  to you you I think were the first people  to bring fiber into the French market  and you're a real you're really really  innovator aren't you yeah we started our  fiber project back in 2006 so it is been  a long journey between pushing the right  regulation putting in place to the  processes but today we are the number  one alternative operator in terms of  fiber in France we have 10 million  connectable circuits we have a 3,000  employees dedicated to the rollout of  fiber in France and on top of that we  are the number one alternative operator  in terms of subscriber it took us 12  years to get the first million of  subscribers and 2018 is really a year of  transition a year of an acceleration  because we increase that one number of  subscribers by 50% and if it took us 12  years to get the first million of  subscribers it will take us only 18  months to get the second million so we  are in that unique moment in time in the  history of a French fiber I think you  were saying the opening of the French  market has helped give us an update on  the French to the regulatory position  yes so it's a very interesting mechanism  we have basically a three different  footprints the dance zone we all invest  on our own and in the medium and low  density zone there is a co-investment  mechanism so clearly so far the opening  of the French telecom market has been a  success  in terms of purchasing power for the  citizens in terms of reducing the  digital divide in terms also of  investment cycle but we should pay  attention on the right implementation of  the of that regulation and as you move  forward what for you are some of the  next challenges fiber is still a big  challenge and we have to pay a lot of  attention regarding the implementation  of that regulation specifically in the  co-investment scheme because in some  cases the co investment is done for  example with the incumbent and then in  combat as strengthen its position thanks  to fiber recently and so we pay a lot of  attention to two topics  there should be no operational  discrimination and the equivalents of  input is very important and two we  consider also that there should be a  Chinese wall between the world cell team  in charge of the co-investment mechanism  and they have a clear view of where we  invest and the retail team of the  incumbent so this is a clear topic for  us clearly for us fiber is the number  one strategic topic we do believe in the  future of fiber but we need to have a  proper regulation and we need also that  strong political will on that topic okay  well thank you very much for joining us  today thank you Brian  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

